---
const articles = [
  {
    tag: "NEW THIS WEEK",
    title:
      "Researchers found another clue about why endometriosis causes chronic pain.",
    excerpt:
      "A new study explores how inflammatory signalling may contribute to persistent pain in endometriosis — and what the findings actually mean.",
    readTime: "6 MIN READ",
  },
  {
    tag: "RESEARCH BREAKDOWN",
    title:
      "What scientists are learning about progesterone resistance in endometriosis.",
    excerpt:
      "Why some endometrial tissue responds differently to hormonal signalling, explained without the jargon.",
    readTime: "5 MIN READ",
  },
  {
    tag: "WOMEN'S HEALTH",
    title:
      "Why a promising biomarker study does not automatically mean a new diagnostic test.",
    excerpt:
      "A useful reminder of the difference between exciting early research and something ready for clinical practice.",
    readTime: "7 MIN READ",
  },
];
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Endocation translates endometriosis and women's health research into language that actually makes sense."
    />
    <title>Endocation</title>

    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link
      href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Manrope:wght@400;500;600;700;800&display=swap"
      rel="stylesheet"
    />
  </head>

  <body>
    <header class="site-header">
    <a href="/" class="brand">
  <img src="/endocation-logo.png" alt="Endocation logo" class="brand-logo" />
  <span>ENDOCATION</span>
</a>

      <nav>
  <a href="/research" data-astro-reload>Latest Research</a>
  <a href="/endometriosis-101" data-astro-reload>Endometriosis 101</a>
  <a href="/advocate" data-astro-reload>Advocate</a>
  <a href="/about" data-astro-reload>About</a>
  <a href="/contact" data-astro-reload>Contact</a>
</nav>
    </header>

    <main>
      <section class="hero">
        <div class="hero-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">ENDOMETRIOSIS · WOMEN'S HEALTH · SCIENCE</p>

          <h1>
            The research is complicated.
            <span>Your health shouldn't be.</span>
          </h1>

          <p class="hero-description">
            Endometriosis and women's health research translated into language
            that actually makes sense — so you can understand the evidence,
            ask better questions and advocate for your health.
          </p>

          <div class="hero-actions">
            <a href="/research" class="button primary">Read the latest</a>
<a href="/endometriosis-101" class="button secondary">Start with the basics</a>
          </div>

          <p class="weekly">NEW RESEARCH BREAKDOWN EVERY WEEK</p>
        </div>

        <div class="hero-card">
          <span class="mini-label">WHY ENDOCATION?</span>
          <p>
            Because understanding your health shouldn't require a biomedical
            degree.
          </p>

          <div class="scribble">↘</div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="research section" id="research">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">THE LATEST</p>
            <h2>This week in women's health.</h2>
          </div>

          <a href="/research" class="text-link">View all research →</a>
        </div>

        <div class="article-grid">
          {
            articles.map((article, index) => (
              <article class:list={["article-card", { featured: index === 0 }]}>
                <div class="article-meta">
                  <span>{article.tag}</span>
                  <span>{article.readTime}</span>
                </div>

                <h3>{article.title}</h3>
                <p>{article.excerpt}</p>

                <a href="/research" class="article-link">Read the breakdown →</a>
              </article>
            ))
          }
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="breakdown section">
        <div class="breakdown-intro">
          <p class="eyebrow yellow">THE ENDOCATION BREAKDOWN</p>
          <h2>Reading research shouldn't require a biomedical degree.</h2>
          <p>
            Every Endocation article is designed to separate what a paper
            actually found from what the headlines might make you think it
            found.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="breakdown-steps">
          <div>
            <span>01</span>
            <h3>What did they find?</h3>
            <p>The actual result, minus the academic language.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <span>02</span>
            <h3>How good is the evidence?</h3>
            <p>Study design, sample size and the context that matters.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <span>03</span>
            <h3>What doesn't it prove?</h3>
            <p>Because interesting research is not the same as certainty.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <span>04</span>
            <h3>What could this mean for you?</h3>
            <p>Questions and context to help you understand your care.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="basics section" id="basics">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">START HERE</p>
            <h2>Endometriosis 101.</h2>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="basics-grid">
          <article class="basic-card intro-card">
            <p class="mini-label">THE BIG QUESTION</p>
            <h3>Okay... what actually is endometriosis?</h3>
            <p>
              A jargon-free introduction to what's happening in the body and
              what researchers are still trying to understand.
            </p>
            <a href="/endometriosis-101">Learn the basics →</a>
          </article>

          <article class="basic-card">
            <span>01</span>
            <h3>Symptoms</h3>
            <p>More than “just bad periods.”</p>
          </article>

          <article class="basic-card">
            <span>02</span>
            <h3>Diagnosis</h3>
            <p>What actually happens and what different tests can tell you.</p>
          </article>

          <article class="basic-card">
            <span>03</span>
            <h3>Treatment</h3>
            <p>Understanding your options without being told what to choose.</p>
          </article>

          <article class="basic-card">
            <span>04</span>
            <h3>The science</h3>
            <p>Hormones, inflammation, pain signalling and more.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="advocate section" id="advocate">
        <div class="advocate-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">ADVOCATE</p>
          <h2>You deserve to understand the conversation.</h2>
          <p>
            Practical resources to help you prepare for appointments, describe
            your symptoms clearly, understand medical terminology and ask
            informed questions.
          </p>

          <a href="/advocate" class="button primary">Explore advocacy resources</a>
        </div>

        <div class="advocate-list">
          <div>
            <span>01</span>
            <p>Preparing for an appointment</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <span>02</span>
            <p>How to communicate your symptoms</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <span>03</span>
            <p>Questions you might want to ask</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <span>04</span>
            <p>Understanding medical terminology</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <span>05</span>
            <p>Getting a second opinion</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="about section" id="about">
  <div class="about-copy">
    <p class="eyebrow">BEHIND ENDOCATION</p>

    <h2>Hi, I'm Anoushka.</h2>

    <p class="about-lead">
      I started Endocation because women's health research shouldn't only be
      understandable to the people working in the lab.
    </p>

    <div class="about-divider"></div>

    <p>
      I have an MSc in <strong>Genetic Manipulation and Molecular Cell Biology</strong>.
      My background spans molecular and cell biology and global health, and
      Endocation sits right in the middle: translating research, questioning
      what the evidence actually shows and making science more useful to the
      people it affects.
    </p>

    <a href="/about">My story →</a>
  </div>

  <div class="about-image-wrap">
    <img
      src="/anoushka-lab.jpg"
      alt="Anoushka in a molecular biology laboratory"
      class="about-image"
    />


  </div>
</section>

     

      <section class="contact section" id="contact">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">CONTACT & COLLABORATIONS</p>
          <h2>Let's work together.</h2>
          <p>
            Researcher, organisation, patient advocate or science communicator?
            I'd love to hear from you.
          </p>
        </div>

        <a href="/contact" class="button primary">
          Get in touch
        </a>
      </section>
	  
	  <section class="newsletter">
  <div class="newsletter-inner">
    <div class="newsletter-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">THE ENDOCATION NEWSLETTER</p>

      <h2>New research.<br /><span>Without the jargon.</span></h2>

      <p>
        Get the latest Endocation research breakdown straight to your inbox.
        One email when a new article drops. No spam, just the science.
      </p>
    </div>

    <form
      class="newsletter-form"
      name="newsletter"
      method="POST"
      data-netlify="true"
      netlify-honeypot="bot-field"
      action="/newsletter-success"
    >
      <input type="hidden" name="form-name" value="newsletter" />

      <p class="newsletter-hidden">
        <label>
          Don't fill this out:
          <input name="bot-field" />
        </label>
      </p>

      <label for="newsletter-name">First name</label>
      <input
        id="newsletter-name"
        type="text"
        name="name"
        placeholder="Your first name"
      />

      <label for="newsletter-email">Email</label>
      <input
        id="newsletter-email"
        type="email"
        name="email"
        placeholder="you@email.com"
        required
      />

      <button type="submit">Keep me in the loop →</button>

      <p class="newsletter-small">
        Unsubscribe anytime. Your inbox deserves boundaries too.
      </p>
    </form>
  </div>
</section>
    </main>

    <footer>
     <a href="/" class="brand footer-brand">
  <img
    src="/endocation-logo.png"
    alt="Endocation logo"
    class="brand-logo"
  />
  <span>ENDOCATION</span>
</a>

      <p>
        Evidence-led women's health education. Not individual medical advice.
      </p>

      <p class="copyright">© 2026 ENDOCATION</p>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>

